1. Investigate and Fix Customer Auto-Logout

Currently, customers are automatically logged out from the web application after some time. Investigate the actual root cause and fix it properly.

Check the existing:

- JWT authentication and token expiration.
- Access token and refresh token handling, if implemented.
- Authentication middleware.
- Axios interceptors.
- API error handling.
- Frontend authentication state.
- React state/context management.
- Page refresh behaviour.
- Socket.IO connection/disconnection behaviour.
- Browser session handling.
- LocalStorage/sessionStorage usage.
- Backend token validation.
- Cookie settings, if used.
- Concurrent API requests when token expires.
- Deployment-related authentication issues.

Required behaviour

- Customers should remain logged in until their actual authentication session expires or they explicitly logout.
- Avoid unnecessary logout caused by page refresh, navigation, temporary network failure, backend restart or Socket.IO disconnection.
- If refresh token functionality already exists, fix and reuse it.
- If access and refresh token architecture is appropriate but missing, implement a secure refresh-token mechanism using the existing backend conventions.
- Automatically refresh expired access tokens where a valid refresh session exists.
- If multiple API requests receive an expired access token simultaneously, prevent multiple simultaneous refresh requests.
- Queue or retry eligible failed requests after successful token refresh.
- Do not create an infinite retry loop.
- If refresh fails because the session is genuinely expired or revoked, log the user out safely and show a clear message.
- Do not log out users because of temporary server/network errors.
- Persist authentication state appropriately across browser refreshes.
- Do not store sensitive authentication data insecurely.
- Never expose refresh tokens or secrets in logs.
- Respect explicit logout and server-side session revocation.
- Ensure role-based authentication remains intact for Admin, Organizer, Scorer, Team Captain and Customer.

Security

- Do not simply increase token expiry to an unnecessarily long duration or remove authentication expiry validation.
- Implement a secure session persistence strategy.
- Investigate the root cause before modifying the authentication system.
- Maintain proper server-side authorization.

