4. Fix Uploaded Document/Image Preview in Admin Approval Panel

Currently, when Admin opens an uploaded document, image or file link while checking a team/application for approval, the preview does not appear above all other components.

Investigate and fix the actual issue.

Check:

- Modal/dialog z-index.
- Parent component stacking contexts.
- CSS transform creating stacking contexts.
- Positioning and overflow properties.
- Sidebar and navbar z-index.
- Dropdown and popover stacking contexts.
- Image preview overlay.
- PDF preview overlay.
- Browser download behaviour.
- Existing file preview components.

Required behaviour

When Admin or Organizer clicks an uploaded document, image or file link:

- Open the preview on top of the entire application.
- The preview must be visible above the sidebar, navbar, cards, dialogs, dropdowns and all other UI components.
- Use a proper modal/lightbox overlay.
- The background should have a dark translucent overlay.
- Preview content must remain properly centered.
- The preview must be responsive.
- It must work on desktop and mobile.
- Ensure proper z-index and stacking context handling.
- Prevent the preview from being clipped by parent containers.
- Close preview using the close button.
- Close preview using Escape where appropriate.
- Clicking outside the preview should close it where appropriate.
- Do not break the underlying approval workflow.

Image Preview

For image files:

- Display a large image preview.
- Support zoom or open-in-new-tab functionality where appropriate.
- Provide a close button.
- Prevent image overflow on small screens.

PDF Preview

For PDFs:

- Display the PDF inside an appropriate responsive preview modal.
- Use the browser PDF viewer or the existing PDF preview library.
- Provide open-in-new-tab or download functionality where appropriate.
- Ensure PDF preview is not hidden behind other UI components.

Other File Types

For unsupported document formats:

- Show the file name and file type.
- Provide an appropriate open/download option.
- Do not pretend the file is previewable if it is not.

Technical Requirements for Preview Layer

- Use a proper modal portal to render the preview at the root level of the application where appropriate, such as React Portal.
- Avoid stacking context issues caused by nested containers.
- Ensure modal z-index is higher than all existing application layers.
- Do not just increase z-index randomly without fixing the stacking context issue.
- Preserve the existing file URLs and upload workflow.
- Do not re-upload files unnecessarily.
- Do not break approval, rejection or verification functionality.

